  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This pull request bounds the -bytespersigop parameter at node startup to [0, 21474] and checks the transaction sigop cost limit before staging transactions in the mempool changeset. Currently, unbounded parameter values or transactions with excessive sigops cause arithmetic overflow when computing sigop-adjusted int32 sizes, triggering debug assertion crashes in fee rate calculations and TxGraphImpl::AddTransaction. The author demonstrates that at -bytespersigop=21474, an incoming transaction with 100,040 sigops overflows INT32_MAX and aborts debug nodes during staging prior to being rejected. The PR requires no external dependencies.",
